tyl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trotyl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trotyl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trotyl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trotyl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trotyl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-01-04T02:32:19Z","updated_at":"2018-01-04T06:48:30Z","body":"@ocombe It's a general bug for named format retrieval, in [data-extracting process](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/0f5c70d563b6943623a5940036a52fe077ad3fac/tools/gulp-tasks/cldr/extract.js#L291-L296), there's a `removeDuplicates` function used to get rid of extra bytes, but **there're [no corresponding fallback logic](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/4ec5e282d9dc842ba430077f0f8e32cebbf7fcbc/packages/common/src/i18n/locale_data_api.ts#L254-L257) for reusing removed formats at runtime**.\r\n\r\nIn this case, `zh` locale [provide same formats](https://github.com/unicode-cldr/cldr-dates-full/blob/3eb9156b699ee903805411c37a63afc7f3594349/main/zh/ca-generic.json#L312-L313) for `mediumDate` & `longDate`, so the latter is stripped. And then no `longDate` named format found at runtime, making it being regarded as a normal format.\r\n  ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/355183908/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"trotyl","id":6059170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTkxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6059170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/trotyl","html_url":"https://github.com/trotyl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trotyl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/use